        },
        "subject": "LU-20611 lfs: name the unrecognized find option",
        "message": "LU-20611 lfs: name the unrecognized find option\n\nlfs find printed argv[optind - 1] for an unknown option.  When the\nbad character is inside a word, such as 'x' in -lxy, getopt has\nnot moved optind past that word, so the message named the word\nbefore it, often the search path.  Print the word getopt was in.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie141cfa961b48005e11aee8c9429dbc6a2452eac\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
